From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nds-ports <nds-ports@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:09:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add a Nintendo DS build

Makefile.nds builds a DSi enhanced .nds with devkitARM and libnds/calico,
with int sized enums like Quake expects and common symbols for the
globals it defines in headers. The collision code, memcpy and memset and
libgcc's software floating point, which Quake uses everywhere as the
ARM9 has no floating point unit, run from ITCM as ARM code: the floating
point objects are taken out of libgcc with their code moved to ITCM and
linked before it. Constants are single precision, so expressions like
x * 0.5 don't go through double precision. HOT_CODE puts single
functions in ITCM, the rest is Thumb code in main RAM: the QuakeC
interpreter, BoxOnPlaneSide, Mod_PointInLeaf, RecursiveLightPoint and
R_DrawParticles. The float comparisons come from fcmp_nds.s instead of
libgcc, whose comparisons take three calls and save five registers.
